<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Erythraean Sibyl</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sibyl of Erythrae</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Erythraean Sibyl was a legendary prophetess of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> associated with Erythrae, an Ionian city on the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a> opposite Chios. Ancient writers counted her among the most famous of the sibyls, and verses ascribed to her circulated widely. Christian writers later read her prophecies as foretelling Christ, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michelangelo">Michelangelo</a> painted her on the ceiling of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sistine-chapel">Sistine Chapel</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/erythraean-sibyl.jpg" alt="Erythraean Sibyl" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michelangelo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Erythraean.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
